before:
Use a small known code to classify an expected failure.
```javascript
const problem = {code: "MISSING_FIELD", message: "internal details"};
console.log(problem.code === "MISSING_FIELD");
```

Place error middleware after routes that may fail.
```javascript
app.use((error, req, res, next) => {
  if (res.headersSent) return next(error);
  res.status(500).json({error: "Request failed"});
});
```

after:
```javascript
function errorReply(error) {
  if (error?.code === "INVALID_INPUT") {
    return {status: 400, body: {error: "Check the supplied values"}};
  }
  return {status: 500, body: {error: "Something went wrong"}};
}
console.log(errorReply({code: "INVALID_INPUT", message: "private details"}));
```
This returns status 400 with the public message Check the supplied values.
